# Accepted-risk register for Trivy dependency findings.
# Each entry expires (exp:) so it comes back up for review instead of being
# silenced for good. Flat format on purpose: CI runs `trivy fs` without
# --ignorefile, which loads `.trivyignore` by default (not `.trivyignore.yaml`).
# Matching is by vulnerability id across every package and path, not per
# package: when reviewing, check each id still hits only the package named
# below (verified for all four on 2026-11-02).
# Accepted 2026-11-02 (security scan, reachability reviewed in the iterate
# iterate-2026-11-02-security-accept-findings).

# react-router 6.30.6: open redirect via backslashes in <Link>/useNavigate.
# Not reachable: every navigation target is a fixed literal path
# ("/", "/info", "/settings"); no link is built from user input.
# Fix needs react-router 7 (major upgrade).
CVE-2026-53669 exp:2027-05-01

# react-router 6.30.6: constructor injection in deserializeErrors() during SSR
# hydration. Not reachable: client-only SPA (HashRouter), no server rendering.
# Fix needs react-router 7 (major upgrade).
CVE-2026-53666 exp:2027-05-01

# glob and minimatch below are listed as production packages in
# package-lock.json only because tailwindcss-animate (a dependency) declares
# tailwindcss (a devDependency) as a peer; nothing in src/ imports them.

# glob 10.5.0 (tailwindcss > sucrase > glob): DoS via incomplete traversal
# cancellation. Build-time only, never shipped to the browser; the patterns it
# walks come from our own Tailwind config. Fix needs glob 14 (major, unsupported
# by sucrase).
CVE-2026-118773 exp:2027-05-01

# minimatch 9.0.9 (tailwindcss > sucrase > glob > minimatch): DoS via crafted
# glob pattern expansion. Build-time only; patterns are developer-authored, not
# attacker-controlled. Fix needs minimatch 11 (major, unsupported upstream).
CVE-2026-118764 exp:2027-05-01
